<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY'S SKALA TO SELL OWN SHARES IN Q1.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY'S SKALA TO SELL OWN SHARES IN Q1.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Skala-Coop Rt said on Wednesday that it planned to sell 10,000 own shares in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The company did not provide further details on its plans.</p>
<p>In the past three days Skala shares remained untraded on the Budapest Stock Exchange but on January 16 they closed at 1,900 forints.</p>
<p>Skala is a holding company, majority-owned by Germany's Tengelmann AG.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
